          "id": "SP_OOPELTA_CAPENSIS_POLLONERA_1909",
          "name": "Oopelta capensis Pollonera, 1909",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Oopelta",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Green-yellow to green-gray body, spots and lines of red-brown on dorsum and sides; greyish white body in alcohol; black spots on the mantle and dorsum of some specimens, others have just tiny dark spots on mantle and sometimes dorsum and sides; red-brown granules on mantle; pale foot fringe; sole and head yellowish or green-gray; eggs 3-3.5 mm diameter; blue-green slime (!) and possible reddish slime when irritated (van Bruggen in Altena 1966; Altena 1966).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Calcium carbonate granules as vestigial shell; no apparent epiphallus; large atrium (Altena 1966).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9671310",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "8b04a87d-8a77-5fe-971-7049835fbb1e08",
