        {
          "id": "SP_ARIOSTRALIS_NEBULOSA_SIRGEL_1985",
          "name": "Ariostralis nebulosa Sirgel, 1985",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Ariostralis",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Black, dark gray, or brown-gray body; rounded backside without keel; hexagonal tubercles on skin; clear, sticky mucus; 1-part sole, body width or wider, remaining wide and flat when the animal is contracted (Sirgel 1985).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\"> </p><p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Internal shell 4.0 x 2.2. mm; pigmented ovotestis; penis with four sections: short basal apical section attached to vas deferens and retractor muscle and with an internal papilla, wider section and third sections containing calcareous spines with one very large spine, and fourth, basal section long and thin; vagina and oviduct longer than atrium; upper portion of vagina in the shape of a bulb, attached to spermatheca duct; vaginal bulb with a second inner cartilaginous wall attached by strands to outer wall; long spermatheca duct passes around base of retractor muscles and to albumen gland; very short atrium (Sirgel 1985).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:8959767",
          "authorship": "Sirgel",
          "yearPublished": "1985",
          "children": [],
